Rule 1 (operands must both be boolean or both integral tensors)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (dtype_(v_1) = 0 ∧ dtype_(v_2) = 0) ∨ (1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5 ∧ 1 ≤ dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 5)
>>
Rule 2 (tensor-tensor operands must be broadcastable)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∨ shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = 1
>>
Rule 3 (out tensor dtype must match result and be supported)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 0 ∧ dtype_(v_2) = 0 then dtype_(v_3) = 0 else (1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5 ∧ 1 ≤ dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 5 ∧ dtype_(v_3) = dtype_(v_1))
>>
Rule 4 (out tensor shape must match result; no mismatch on any dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ndim(v_3) = ndim(v_1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∧ shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_1, i)
